      "writtenOn": "2016-12-16T02:49:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This interface seems error-prone. In particular, it makes the caller responsible for ensuring that no one is writing to |registered_|, at the time of access to the vector.\n\n\nSignificantly, that \"access to the vector\" could occur not just at the time that getRegistrations() is called, but anytime there-after.\n\n\nWhile the current calling code is correct, I think it\u0027ll be hard for us to maintain that correctness as we modify this file.\n\n\nCan we, instead, have the class itself ensure thread-safety? I imagine something like:\n- move the last block of code from startSupplicantAndWaitForHidlService to this method\n- change the name of this method to waitForHidlService()\n- move the synchronization objects to the private section\n\nIf we did that, then I believe the object would be thread-safe. (Famous last words, I\u0027m sure.)",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 70,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 70,
        "endChar": 33
      },
      "revId": "6b355d45a451a3bf6fe307f6766ac3762dfe4e82",
